  "result": "Subcommands now pick up their defaults from `default_map`. The full suite passes (1907 passed, 102 skipped, 1 xfailed).\n\n**Cause:** in `Context.__init__` (`src/click/core.py`, around line 392), a child context inherited its parent's whole `default_map`. A subcommand named `sub` therefore looked up `name` at the top level of the map instead of under `default_map[\"sub\"]`.\n\n**Fix:** the child context now takes `parent.default_map.get(info_name)`, so it gets its own section of the map.\n\n**Test:** I added `test_default_map_subcommand` in `tests/test_defaults.py`. It runs a group with one subcommand and `default_map={\"sub\": {\"name\": \"mapped\"}}`, and checks the subcommand prints `mapped`. I did not run it against the unfixed code to confirm it fails there.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
